{"id": "money-the-ledger-stops-following", "title": "Stipends through a bank, gift cards, intermediaries: money the ledger stops following", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.107, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "502676ee1bf7d38e", "words": 367, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "Who gets the stipends San Francisco pays people in its programs?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.29, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Stipends", "sub": "small payments to people in City programs"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.44, 0.55, 1.1, 1.33, 1.87, 2.2, 2.53, 2.63, 2.8]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The biggest payee isn’t a person. It’s a bank, US Bank. How much?", "t0": 4.29, "t1": 9.76, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The largest payee", "sub": "the City’s “Stipends” account"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.57, 1.03, 1.26, 1.33, 2.27, 2.51, 2.59, 3.28, 3.66, 4.61, 4.85]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "oneLine"], "text": "7.7 million dollars.", "t0": 9.76, "t1": 11.64, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$7.7 million", "label": "stipends paid to US Bank National Association", "sub": "$7.1 million from Economic & Workforce Development, fiscal 2021 to 2025"}, "emph": ["7.7"], "wt": [0.04, 0.39, 0.67, 0.96, 1.32]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 12.16, "t1": 13.72, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.41, 0.76, 0.93, 1.01]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "A bank can pay many people at once.", "t0": 13.84, "t1": 15.77, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Economic & Workforce Development", "sub": "stipends"}, {"art": "money", "name": "US Bank National Association", "sub": "the payee on file"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Who received them?", "sub": "how many people, in what form: not in the file"}], "kicker": "Where the trail ends"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.44, 0.6, 0.8, 1.02, 1.33, 1.48]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "But then the file shows only the bank. Not who, or how many.", "t0": 15.89, "t1": 19.39, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Economic & Workforce Development", "sub": "stipends"}, {"art": "money", "name": "US Bank National Association", "sub": "the payee on file"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Who received them?", "sub": "how many people, in what form: not in the file"}], "kicker": "Where the trail ends"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.4, 0.73, 1.04, 1.37, 1.47, 2.08, 2.37, 2.74, 2.97, 3.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The Police Department used the same route:", "t0": 19.51, "t1": 21.52, "shot": "b4p", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Police Department", "sub": "$516,498 in stipends paid to the bank, fiscal 2024 to 2026; no contract number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.44, 0.9, 1.09, 1.2, 1.47]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "516,498 dollars, with no contract number on file.", "t0": 21.52, "t1": 26.76, "shot": "b4p", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Police Department", "sub": "$516,498 in stipends paid to the bank, fiscal 2024 to 2026; no contract number"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.4, 0.76, 1.26, 1.73, 2.0, 2.34, 2.85, 3.37, 3.63, 3.86, 4.37, 4.66, 4.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why", "established[0]"], "text": "Next, gift cards: cash, once they leave the drawer.", "t0": 26.98, "t1": 29.91, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.79, 1.32, 1.84, 2.08, 2.24, 2.45, 2.53]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why", "established[0]"], "text": "Three Controller audits found records too thin to account for every card.", "t0": 30.03, "t1": 33.84, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "emph": ["too thin"], "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.82, 1.22, 1.48, 1.9, 2.15, 2.46, 2.58, 2.95, 3.11, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Human Services bought 2.8 million dollars of cards.", "t0": 33.96, "t1": 37.18, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.82, 1.07, 1.29, 1.56, 1.8, 2.15, 2.5, 2.61]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "One program used 1 of the 500 it got.", "t0": 37.3, "t1": 39.7, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "emph": ["1 of the 500"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.74, 0.92, 1.07, 1.15, 1.26, 1.53, 1.88, 1.99]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "At the Human Rights Commission, 20,507 dollars of cards had no proof of purchase.", "t0": 39.82, "t1": 45.54, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Three Controller audits of gift cards", "rows": [["Human Services Agency", "$2.8 million"], ["Public Health", "$487,060"], ["Human Rights Commission", "$20,507"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.29, 0.57, 0.84, 1.41, 1.8, 2.28, 2.61, 2.97, 3.31, 3.67, 3.78, 4.21, 4.41, 4.62, 4.93, 5.06]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[1]", "next[4]"], "text": "And purchase codes miss prepaid debit cards, like Visa ReliaCards. So the full total isn’t known.", "t0": 45.66, "t1": 51.86, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Visa ReliaCards, which are prepaid debit cards"}, "emph": ["isn’t known"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.56, 0.92, 1.15, 1.63, 1.9, 2.53, 2.76, 3.05, 4.59, 4.79, 4.88, 5.15, 5.55, 5.81]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Then, intermediaries: contracts that pay someone to pass money on.", "t0": 52.08, "t1": 57.03, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City department", "sub": "pays"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Fiscal intermediary, agent or sponsor", "sub": "paid to pass money on"}, {"art": "question", "name": "People or a named project", "sub": "not in the payment file"}], "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 2.13, 2.72, 2.9, 3.15, 3.46, 3.54, 3.84, 4.14]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "How much since 2019?", "t0": 57.03, "t1": 59.4, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City department", "sub": "pays"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Fiscal intermediary, agent or sponsor", "sub": "paid to pass money on"}, {"art": "question", "name": "People or a named project", "sub": "not in the payment file"}], "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.56, 0.85, 1.17]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "amount"], "text": "111.5 million dollars.", "t0": 59.4, "t1": 61.99, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$111.5 million", "label": "paid since fiscal 2019 to 19 payees"}, "emph": ["111.5"], "wt": [0.04, 0.28, 0.62, 0.98, 1.27, 1.6, 1.98]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Healthright 360 alone got 77.7 million. The record ends there.", "t0": 62.51, "t1": 67.92, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to pass money on, since fiscal 2019", "rows": [["Healthright 360 · fiscal intermediary", "$77.7 million"], ["Abode Services · fiscal agent", "$11.4 million"], ["Community Initiatives · fiscal sponsor", "$7.8 million"], ["San Francisco Study Center Inc", "$5.5 million"]]}, "emph": ["77.7 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 0.71, 1.01, 1.4, 1.79, 1.99, 2.68, 2.96, 3.25, 4.11, 4.3, 4.67, 5.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Community benefit districts are funded by assessments on their own property owners.", "t0": 68.14, "t1": 72.39, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Community benefit districts", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "funded by assessments on their own property owners"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.92, 1.4, 1.56, 1.9, 2.05, 2.66, 2.8, 3.0, 3.22, 3.71]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Yet in 5, City grants came to half that or more.", "t0": 72.51, "t1": 75.37, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.37, 0.82, 1.11, 1.49, 1.73, 1.86, 2.12, 2.34, 2.48]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Excelsior Action Group: 205 percent.", "t0": 75.49, "t1": 78.05, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "emph": ["205 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.88, 1.19, 1.4, 1.76, 2.03]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "City grantees, with boards the City doesn’t appoint.", "t0": 78.17, "t1": 80.98, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Excelsior Action Group", "City grants: 205% of its assessment"], "b": ["Noe Valley Association", "55%"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2023 to 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.99, 1.19, 1.61, 1.73, 2.02, 2.32]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[8]"], "text": "Lower Polk’s district paid 1.4 million dollars to a firm run by its former executive director.", "t0": 81.1, "t1": 86.69, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "cleaning and ambassador services, 3 returns", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.71, 1.21, 1.48, 1.7, 1.98, 2.25, 2.62, 3.04, 3.19, 3.27, 3.58, 3.84, 3.99, 4.17, 4.52, 5.01]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[8]"], "text": "Its own return says so.", "t0": 86.81, "t1": 88.17, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "cleaning and ambassador services, 3 returns", "chip": "$1.4 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.39, 0.76, 1.02]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Last, rent. The Airport, the Port and the Real Estate Division may forgive rent tenant by tenant.", "t0": 88.39, "t1": 94.53, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The Airport, the Port, the Real Estate Division", "sub": "standing authority"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Rent forgiven or reduced", "sub": "tenant by tenant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "no file"}], "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.7, 1.68, 1.87, 2.51, 2.65, 3.07, 3.25, 3.33, 3.53, 3.78, 4.2, 4.4, 4.82, 5.11, 5.48, 5.66]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Those sums are in no Board file.", "t0": 94.65, "t1": 96.42, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The Airport, the Port, the Real Estate Division", "sub": "standing authority"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Rent forgiven or reduced", "sub": "tenant by tenant"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "no file"}], "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.6, 0.75, 0.85, 1.01, 1.32]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The Airport’s own pandemic estimate: 21.8 million dollars. The rest is unknown.", "t0": 96.54, "t1": 102.2, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$21.8 million", "label": "the Airport’s own estimate for its pandemic programme"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.66, 0.92, 1.49, 1.97, 2.57, 2.87, 3.12, 3.5, 4.49, 4.68, 4.99, 5.15]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Two things checked out: charges between departments hold steady, and hospital bad debt is falling.", "t0": 102.42, "t1": 108.28, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["charges between departments", "7.7% of spending, steady"], "b": ["hospital bad debt", "1.3% of gross charges, falling"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.53, 0.86, 1.53, 2.0, 2.32, 2.84, 3.12, 3.84, 4.08, 4.58, 4.88, 5.17, 5.33]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Nothing shows any stipend, card or pass-through payment went to the wrong person.", "t0": 108.5, "t1": 112.6, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any stipend, card or pass-through payment went to the wrong person", "What fee each intermediary kept"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.63, 0.83, 1.53, 1.88, 2.0, 2.52, 2.88, 3.1, 3.19, 3.27, 3.53]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[4]", "next[0]"], "text": "What would settle it? Each department’s gift-card log, and the lists of rent forgiven.", "t0": 112.72, "t1": 117.41, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each department’s gift-card log: bought, issued, on hand, lost"}, {"who": "", "what": "The Port’s and the Airport’s lists of rent forgiven, tenant by tenant"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.31, 0.64, 1.38, 1.68, 2.25, 2.78, 3.17, 3.32, 3.42, 3.7, 3.85, 4.11]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The Boys and Girls Clubs also reported grants together, without naming each recipient.", "t0": 117.53, "t1": 122.06, "shot": "club-records", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Boys & Girls Clubs of San Francisco", "heading": "Grants reported together on Schedule I", "source": "bg2024", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "FY2022", "value": "$536,143"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "FY2023", "value": "$322,199"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "FY2024", "value": "$4,015,709"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.38, 0.48, 0.8, 1.16, 1.53, 1.94, 2.32, 2.83, 3.22, 3.6, 3.85]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[5]"], "text": "The audit confirms the grant total. The filings do not trace City money to those grants.", "t0": 122.18, "t1": 127.2, "shot": "club-funds", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bgAudit2025", "kicker": "Grant disclosures", "text": "The funding source for the grants remains unidentified.", "mark": "funding source"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 0.99, 1.1, 1.41, 2.26, 2.43, 2.92, 3.09, 3.28, 3.57, 3.84, 4.11, 4.22, 4.46]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.32, "t1": 129.4, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.41, 0.52, 0.58, 1.04, 1.23, 1.31]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Lead 1 · gift cards", "lead2": "Lead 2 · intermediaries", "lead3": "Lead 3 · benefit districts",